{
  "opening": "The boltons library is releasing new functionality and fixes that the glom consumer relies on for data restructuring and error handling. To ensure compatibility and correct behavior, glom must update its dependency to the next boltons release which includes these specific API changes.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "m08",
      "text": "In the boltons project, the OneToOne class must handle non-unique one-to-one inputs without raising errors or losing data integrity. The FastIterOrderedMultiDict and unique utilities must continue to function correctly when processing such inputs."
    },
    {
      "id": "m12",
      "text": "In the boltons project, the FunctionBuilder class must operate without generating Python 3 warnings related to inspect module usage. The public names formatargandannotation, get_module_callables, and inspect_formatargspec must remain accessible and functional as part of this vendorized implementation."
    },
    {
      "id": "m12c",
      "text": "In the boltons project, observed through glom's tests, the FunctionBuilder class must operate without generating Python 3 warnings related to inspect module usage. The public names formatargandannotation, get_module_callables, and inspect_formatargspec must remain accessible and functional as part of this vendorized implementation."
    },
    {
      "id": "m19",
      "text": "In the boltons project, the complement-set utility must support the __rsub__ method for better interoperability with the builtin set type. This ensures that difference_update operations involving sets behave consistently with standard Python set semantics."
    }
  ],
  "closing": "Please verify that these observable behaviors are met in the integration between glom and the updated boltons version."
}
